
EACH SLAVE HAS 
    Address Register 
        - written after the SlaveAddress, RW transaction
        - Sets which address of the memory is being written or read
    Burst Write/Read transaction
        - the master can burst write/read from the memory starting from the address in the address register 

    Write Operation (No Burst)
        - Master sends {SlaveAddress, W} ---> Address to be written ---> Data to be written in that address
    Read Operation (No Burst)
        - Master sends {SlaveAddress, W} ---> Address to be read ---> Repeated Start ---> Master sends {SlaveAddress, R} ---> Slave Sends the Data found in the specified address in the Addr Register 


    To be implemented:
    Write Operation (With Burst)
        - Master sends {SlaveAddress, W} ---> Address to be written ---> Data1 to be written in that address ---> Data2 on address + 1 ---> Data3 on address + 2 ---> ...
    Read Operation (With Burst)
        - Master sends {SlaveAddress, W} ---> Address to be written ---> {SlaveAddress, R} --->Slave sends Data1 found on address ---> Data2 on address + 1 ---> Data3 on address + 2 ---> ...


    
